  "security_implications": "ctr_we drives AES counter write enables from sp2v_sig_chk[5+:NumSlicesCtr]. A width mismatch (NumSlicesCtr > sp2v_sig_chk width - 5) could cause X propagation, disabling counters and breaking AES encryption/decryption. If sp2v_sig_chk bits are not adequately qualified, glitches may spuriously enable counter writes, leading to counter reuse and confidentiality breach.",
